(584078, 58779, 16388, '<td valign="top">Yeah I know it was crapy but I didnt have my tripod with me I was working at the state fair in florida doing a live broadcast and was thinking about something I could do and I saw this thing all day going up then free falling . I sat there for about 2 hours worknig with it to get the best one but it was still so blury. And I didnt have time to go back and do it the correct way. Oh well onto the next one. :)</td>', 'Yeah I know it was crapy but I didnt have my tripod with me I was working at the state fair in florida doing a live broadcast and was thinking about something I could do and I saw this thing all day going up then free falling . I sat there for about 2 hours worknig with it to get the best one but it was still so blury. And I didnt have time to go back and do it the correct way. Oh well onto the next one. :)', '2004-02-18 00:15:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(584089, 59495, 3569, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments, the shot was lousy and it deserved low scores.  It was an experiment, to see if bad shots do get advise, and I think they do. And this one received good comments. Van</td>', 'Thanks for the comments, the shot was lousy and it deserved low scores.  It was an experiment, to see if bad shots do get advise, and I think they do. And this one received good comments. Van', '2004-02-18 00:18:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(584138, 58671, 6349, '<td valign="top">Great showing.  Reading your comments on the photo was as delightful as the the photo itself.  I can just picture you running back and forth in the cold, trying not to make footprints while avoiding the motion sensor and getting sick in the process.  I think the effort was well worth it as this is one of my favorite photos in the challenge.  I agree about the footprints.  You should make an edited version where you clone them out.</td>', 'Great showing.  Reading your comments on the photo was as delightful as the the photo itself.  I can just picture you running back and forth in the cold, trying not to make footprints while avoiding the motion sensor and getting sick in the process.  I think the effort was well worth it as this is one of my favorite photos in the challenge.  I agree about the footprints.  You should make an edited version where you clone them out.', '2004-02-18 00:30:29.000000', NULL, 0),
