(584247, 59059, 17075, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. This was my first challenge, so any kind of input is appreciated.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. This was my first challenge, so any kind of input is appreciated.', '2004-02-18 00:57:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(584278, 59654, 4207, '<td valign="top">Thanks everybody for the comments. I''m really suprised that this image came in so low. <br/> <br/>There were some questions about process:<br/>In Photoshop, I Unsharp Masked --&gt; Color balanced ---&gt; (decided to go B&amp;W) Desaturated---&gt; Edited Curves (more of a S curve) ---&gt; Contrast Adj ---&gt; Croped ---&gt; Bordered---&gt;Submit.<br/> <br/>It took some playing with to get this image to to really pop.<br/> <br/>Subject matter: <br/>I thought this fit the challenge because we see a guy standing out front of, from what i could tell, his workplace having a smoke break. If i''ve ever seen anyone "let go" on a regular basis, it''s smokers on their break. That''s the moment when they have time to think and reflect on their concerns. IMHO.<br/> <br/>eh... I like the image.</td>', 'Thanks everybody for the comments. I''m really suprised that this image came in so low.  There were some questions about process:In Photoshop, I Unsharp Masked --> Color balanced ---> (decided to go B&W) Desaturated---> Edited Curves (more of a S curve) ---> Contrast Adj ---> Croped ---> Bordered--->Submit. It took some playing with to get this image to to really pop. Subject matter: I thought this fit the challenge because we see a guy standing out front of, from what i could tell, his workplace having a smoke break. If i''ve ever seen anyone "let go" on a regular basis, it''s smokers on their break. That''s the moment when they have time to think and reflect on their concerns. IMHO. eh... I like the image.', '2004-02-18 01:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(584400, 59660, 14499, '<td valign="top">22nd.... I am pretty wrapped with that. Considering this was literally last minette and I just did 4 or 5 snap shots of letting this wind up car go and then nearly getting sprung (I have been told I am spending way to much time and effort into these comps, so I did it while the wife was in town.). Adjusting the colour and posting an hour before the deadline.<br/> <br/>I was told it looks like I am catching the carI KNOW! I am not blind ;) but the toy is a wind up one and can not go backwards, all my other toy cars are huge and wouldnt fit into my had. <br/> <br/>I also wanted the letting go theme to have a more significant meaning for this picture hence the Slow Down  Stop holding on so tight title which translates to. I am addicted to speed and I need to let go hence the fast WRX :)  I was going to make the title letting go of the chance of my dream drive but hell! I am driving one so it wouldnt make sense.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the votes.<br/> <br/>Andrew<br/></td>', '22nd.... I am pretty wrapped with that. Considering this was literally last minette and I just did 4 or 5 snap shots of letting this wind up car go and then nearly getting sprung (I have been told I am spending way to much time and effort into these comps, so I did it while the wife was in town.). Adjusting the colour and posting an hour before the deadline. I was told it looks like I am catching the carI KNOW! I am not blind ;) but the toy is a wind up one and can not go backwards, all my other toy cars are huge and wouldnt fit into my had.  I also wanted the letting go theme to have a more significant meaning for this picture hence the Slow Down  Stop holding on so tight title which translates to. I am addicted to speed and I need to let go hence the fast WRX :)  I was going to make the title letting go of the chance of my dream drive but hell! I am driving one so it wouldnt make sense. Thanks for the votes. Andrew', '2004-02-18 01:40:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(584438, 59466, 14499, '<td valign="top">Dude! Hello fellow ozzie as this is your first I thought I would say that the picture could have got a top placing if it had been of better quality. Also I think you are being overly critical of some of the comments.. For example some of the comments are dam near the same and yet you havent ticked them as helpful and may be misconstrued as you thought it was a rude comment.<br/> <br/>Andrew (VIC)</td>', 'Dude! Hello fellow ozzie as this is your first I thought I would say that the picture could have got a top placing if it had been of better quality. Also I think you are being overly critical of some of the comments.. For example some of the comments are dam near the same and yet you havent ticked them as helpful and may be misconstrued as you thought it was a rude comment. Andrew (VIC)', '2004-02-18 01:56:26.000000', NULL, 0),
